  "evidence": [
    "Original identities 5D4E40,60E7C0,60D1B0,605370 are nonvirtual cleanup methods. Imported mangled names are reconstructed, not proof. Physical caller audit found no EAX consumer for checked GraphicWin direct/tail paths, all19 CheckBox and21 RadioButton direct callers, and83 decoded Scroll direct callers; no Scroll tail caller. Linear-sweep boundary evidence and bounded liveness are not whole-game runtime proof.",
    "Current uint32 results manufacture callback-default and deleted-Buffer-pointer values and propagate them through three derived methods. Authorize void contracts and call-discard source while retaining every original reset, callback, deletion and ownership-clear ordering, including unsafe paths. Preserve separately used field_A0C_value getter. Do not sweep unrelated close methods, layout or virtual tables.",
    "Keep ORIGINAL mappings and historical byte claims intact. Update emitted symbol bindings through package source APIs where required, never rewrite ORIGINAL markers. Coordinator permits temporary matching regressions from this justified structural correction, with explicit restoration obligations and actual-source behavioral tests; no automatic acceptance, demotion, score hacks or deliberate bug fixes.",
    "Observe all mapped functions in four owners and affected compiled header consumers. Independent review, relevant host controls, native build/link, claim/reference checks and compiled collateral review precede manual integration. Existing tests asserting incidental numeric returns must become lifecycle/order controls, not simply lose assertions."
  ],
  "intent": "Recover ordinary void lifecycle contracts for GraphicWin close and its CheckBox, RadioButton and Scroll return relays without manufacturing numeric register residue.",
